{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/577034-argentum-and-generic-monsters","id":577034,"title":"Argentum and Generic Monsters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-02T20:36:46-07:00","id":577034,"title":"Argentum and Generic Monsters","content":"So I don't know if everyone has heard, but in Wod Second Edition there will be dread powers included for doing it yourself monsters in a game, ala hunter.<br /> <br /> That made me think, has anyone run or played in a promethean game that included do it yourself monsters ala hunter with a promethean mystic?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T21:56:08-07:00","id":577072,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I had just been using Transmutations to build generic monsters. They're <i>really</i> varied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T22:13:04-07:00","id":577080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/577034-argentum-and-generic-monsters#post577034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I don't know if everyone has heard, but in Wod Second Edition there will be dread powers included for doing it yourself monsters in a game, ala hunter.<br /> <br /> That made me think, has anyone run or played in a promethean game that included do it yourself monsters ala hunter with a promethean mystic?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Surprisingly, even Hunter's monsters tend to fall into categories: if they're using the monster rules from <b>Mortal Remains</b> as a basis, monsters get \u201cmonster templates\u201d which define, amongst other things, what the monster's power stat is. The closest you get to a \u201cgeneric\u201d monster is \u201cthis guy's power stat doesn't match up with any of the ones I know of\u201d. <br /> <br /> I also find myself wondering if PtC2e's Pandorans might end up featuring Dread Powers rather than \u201cPandoran Transmutations\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T23:15:19-07:00","id":577104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/577034-argentum-and-generic-monsters?p=577072#post577072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I had just been using Transmutations to build generic monsters. They're <i>really</i> varied.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough, did any of your do it yourself monster make a lasting enough impression in a game for a mystic to study them, or did you give any thought to a mystic studying them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T23:19:04-07:00","id":577105,"title":"","content":"I've done it with the creatures in Urban Legends, Antagonists and Glimpses of the Unknown.<br /> <br /> Not since 2nd Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T01:50:08-07:00","id":577146,"title":"","content":"I've never run or played in a Promethean game, but I always try to come up with some non-standard monster, just to keep the players from thinking they know everything. I don't really use any particular source to come up with their powers, though, tending to just make something up that sounds cool/suitable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T14:11:07-07:00","id":577753,"title":"","content":"Is WoD 2nd Edition just GM Chronicles reprinted with the full rules, or is it losing the God-Machine details/gaining other detailed story material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:13:25-07:00","id":577827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/577034-argentum-and-generic-monsters?p=577080#post577080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also find myself wondering if PtC2e's Pandorans might end up featuring Dread Powers rather than \u201cPandoran Transmutations\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems the likely course, given Strix and Idigam's precedent, and in light of Centimani losing its status as a Refinement.<br /> <br /> As for Argentum, and I need to go back to the previews, the genericness of a critter shouldn't matter so much as its proximity to humanity. Vampires and mages present Transmutations that are easier to understand and learn, while trafficking with Acamoth or God-Machine Angels may require radical shifts in the paradigm of the Pilgrimage. The major splats each offer their own complex take on what humans are, which is why they are useful to the Mystic. More prosaic beings like the Strix dismiss mortals save when they are useful tools, and are no more sympathetic to the Created. <br /> <br /> If there was more to be learned from the true monsters, I'd imagine it would be how to prey on mortal weakness and vitality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T09:58:54-07:00","id":632447,"title":"","content":"Took Antagonists' variant of the Aswang and made a family of socialites, starlets, supermodels vaguely inpired in the Kardashians with long-standing ties to Abbey Road and the Cheiron Group's board of directors through their brothers, sons and husbands for one of my games, does that count? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Mostly i like to tinker or make riffs on already existing stuff, like turning the Kanaima (from Skinchangers) in a &quot;alternative&quot; to the Strix as &quot;maker/nemesis&quot; of kindred, though i have also used cats (nekomata, or witchcats), serpents and sparrows (in a Shadow of UK-based game) in this role. The sparrows in particular evolved in some scary &quot;crossovery&quot; directions, with ties not only to the Bale Hounds but the Gentry, some lords of the dead <b>and </b>a rivalry with the Strix.<br /> <br /> Have also some lower depths beings that claim to be people that were denied existence and will consume a victim's identity and form to acquire life upon the material world, turning their prey into &quot;ghosts of themselves&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}